#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:4
msgid "Signing packages with OpenSSL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:6
msgid ""
"This is an example of a Package Signing Plugin implementation using the "
"`OpensSSL digest tool <https://docs.openssl.org/3.1/man1/openssl-dgst/>`_. "
"You will need to have ``openssl`` installed at the system level and "
"available in your ``PATH``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:11
msgid ""
"This example is available in the examples2 repository: `examples/extensions/"
"plugins/openssl_sign <https://github.com/conan-io/examples2/tree/main/"
"examples/extensions/plugins/openssl_sign>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:15
msgid ""
"OpenSSL is used here for demonstration purposes only. The Package Signing "
"plugin mechanism is backend-agnostic, and you could implement a similar "
"plugin using other tools available in your system (for example, ``gpg``), "
"with minimal changes to the signing and verification commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:21
msgid "Generating the signing keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:23
msgid ""
"To sign and verify the packages using the plugin, first, we will need a "
"public and private key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:25
msgid "To generate the keys using the ``openssl`` executable, we can run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:27
msgid ""
"$ openssl genpkey -algorithm RSA -out private_key.pem -pkeyopt "
"rsa_keygen_bits:2048"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:31
msgid "This will generate the private key used to sign the packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:33
msgid "Now, we can get the public key from it with this command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:35
msgid "$ openssl pkey -in private_key.pem -pubout -out public_key.pem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:39
msgid "The plugin will use this public key to verify the packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:43
msgid "Configuring the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:47
msgid ""
"This example stores a private key next to the plugin for simplicity. **Do "
"not do this in production**. Instead, load the signing key from environment "
"variables or a secret manager, or delegate signing to a remote signing "
"service. **Always keep the private key out of the Conan cache and out of "
"source control**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:51
msgid ""
"Copy the ``examples/extensions/plugins/openssl_sign/sign.py`` file to your "
"Conan home at ``CONAN_HOME/extensions/plugins/sign/sign.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:53
msgid "Copy the ``sign.py`` file to your Conan home:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:55
msgid "``CONAN_HOME/extensions/plugins/sign/sign.py``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:57
msgid ""
"Place the generated keys in a folder named after your provider (``my-"
"organization`` in this example), next to ``sign.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:60
msgid "Your final folder structure should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:62
msgid ""
"CONAN_HOME/\n"
"└── extensions/\n"
"    └── plugins/\n"
"        └── sign/\n"
"            ├── sign.py\n"
"            └── my-organization/\n"
"                ├── private_key.pem\n"
"                └── public_key.pem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:73
msgid ""
"The ``my-organization`` folder serves as the **provider** in this example, "
"and it is used by the plugin to identify the organization that owns the keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:77
msgid ""
"The Package Signing plugin is installed in the Conan configuration folder, "
"so they can be easily distributed as part of the client configuration using "
"the :ref:`conan config install<reference_commands_conan_config_install>` "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:82
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:84
msgid "The plugin's implementation is very straightforward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:86
msgid ""
"For signing packages, the `sign()` function is defined, where the packages "
"are signed by the :command:`openssl dgst` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:88
msgid ""
"def sign(ref, artifacts_folder, signature_folder, **kwargs)\n"
"    ...\n"
"    openssl_sign_cmd = [\n"
"        \"openssl\",\n"
"        \"dgst\",\n"
"        \"-sha256\",\n"
"        \"-sign\", privkey_filepath,\n"
"        \"-out\", signature_filepath,\n"
"        manifest_filepath\n"
"    ]\n"
"    try:\n"
"        _run_command(openssl_sign_cmd)\n"
"        ConanOutput().success(f\"Package signed for reference {ref}\")\n"
"    except Exception as exc:\n"
"        raise ConanException(f\"Error signing artifact: {exc}\")\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:107
msgid ""
"There, the manifest ``pkgsign-manifest.json`` (created right before "
"``sign()`` function is called) is used to sign the package, as it contains "
"the filenames and checksums of the artifacts of the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:110
msgid ""
"The signature file is saved into the ``signature_filepath`` (the signature "
"folder at ``<package_folder>/metadata/sign``), and finally, the metadata of "
"the signature is returned as a dictionary in a list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:113
msgid ""
"def sign(ref, artifacts_folder, signature_folder, **kwargs)\n"
"    ...\n"
"    return [{\"method\": \"openssl-dgst\",\n"
"         \"provider\": \"my-organization\",\n"
"         \"sign_artifacts\": {\n"
"            \"manifest\": \"pkgsign-manifest.json\",\n"
"            \"signature\": signature_filename}}]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:123
msgid ""
"This information saved in a file ``pkgsign-signatures.json`` placed in the "
"signature folder, so it can be used in the `verify()` to verify the package "
"signature against the correct provider keys, with the correct signing method "
"(``openssl-dgst`` for this example) and using the signature files in "
"``sign_artifacts``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:127
msgid "For verifying packages, the `verify()` function is defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:129
msgid ""
"First, the ``pkgsign-signatures.json`` is loaded to read the metadata of the "
"signatures (multiple signatures are supported):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:131
msgid ""
"def verify(ref, artifacts_folder, signature_folder, files, **kwargs):\n"
"    ...\n"
"    signatures = json.loads(f.read()).get(\"signatures\")\n"
"    ...\n"
"    for signature in signatures:\n"
"        signature_filename = signature.get(\"sign_artifacts\")."
"get(\"signature\")\n"
"        signature_filepath = os.path.join(signature_folder, "
"signature_filename)\n"
"        ...\n"
"        provider = signature.get(\"provider\")\n"
"        signature_method = signature.get(\"method\")\n"
"        ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:145
msgid ""
"Then, the ``provider`` information is used to select the correct public key "
"for verification that use the right signature verification ``method`` "
"(``openssl-dgst`` for this example) and run the :command:`openssl dgst -"
"verify` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:148
msgid ""
"def verify(ref, artifacts_folder, signature_folder, files, **kwargs):\n"
"    ...\n"
"    openssl_verify_cmd = [\n"
"        \"openssl\",\n"
"        \"dgst\",\n"
"        \"-sha256\",\n"
"        \"-verify\", pubkey_filepath,\n"
"        \"-signature\", signature_filepath,\n"
"        manifest_filepath,\n"
"    ]\n"
"    try:\n"
"        _run_command(openssl_verify_cmd)\n"
"        ConanOutput().success(f\"Package verified for reference {ref}\")\n"
"    except Exception as exc:\n"
"        raise ConanException(f\"Error verifying signature "
"{signature_filepath}: {exc}\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:166
msgid ""
"The ``verify()`` function does not return any value in case the package is "
"correct. If the verification fails, then a ``ConanException()`` should be "
"raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:169
msgid "Signing packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:171
msgid ""
"Now that the plugin is configured, we can create a package and sign it "
"afterwards:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:173
msgid ""
"$ conan new cmake_lib -d name=hello -d version=1.0\n"
"$ conan create"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:178
msgid "For signing the recipe and package, use the dedicated command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:180
msgid ""
"$ conan cache sign hello/1.0\n"
"\n"
"hello/1.0: Compressing conan_sources.tgz\n"
"hello/1.0:dee9f7f985eb1c20e3c41afaa8c35e2a34b5ae0b: Compressing "
"conan_package.tgz\n"
"Running command: openssl dgst -sha256 -sign C:\\Users\\user\\."
"conan2\\extensions\\plugins\\sign\\my-organization\\private_key.pem -out C:"
"\\Users\\user\\.conan2\\p\\hello092ffa809a9a1\\d\\metadata\\sign\\pkgsign-"
"manifest.json.sig C:\\Users\\user\\."
"conan2\\p\\hello092ffa809a9a1\\d\\metadata\\sign\\pkgsign-manifest.json\n"
"Package signed for reference hello/1.0\n"
"Running command: openssl dgst -sha256 -sign C:\\Users\\user\\."
"conan2\\extensions\\plugins\\sign\\my-organization\\private_key.pem -out C:"
"\\Users\\user\\.conan2\\p\\b\\hello5b13c694fef4a\\d\\metadata\\sign\\pkgsign-"
"manifest.json.sig C:\\Users\\user\\."
"conan2\\p\\b\\hello5b13c694fef4a\\d\\metadata\\sign\\pkgsign-manifest.json\n"
"Package signed for reference hello/1.0:"
"dee9f7f985eb1c20e3c41afaa8c35e2a34b5ae0b\n"
"[Package sign] Results:\n"
"\n"
"hello/1.0\n"
"revisions\n"
"    53321bba8793db6fea5ea1a98dd6f3d6\n"
"    packages\n"
"        dee9f7f985eb1c20e3c41afaa8c35e2a34b5ae0b\n"
"        revisions\n"
"            4b1eaf2e27996cb39cb3774f185fcd8e\n"
"\n"
"[Package sign] Summary: OK=2, FAILED=0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:202
msgid ""
"As you see, the command is executing the ``sign()`` function of the plugin "
"that uses the ``openssl`` executable to sign the recipe and the package with "
"a command similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:204
msgid ""
"$ openssl dgst -sha256 -sign private_key.pem -out pkgsign-manifest.json.sig "
"pkgsign-manifest.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:208
msgid ""
"And it is also using the conan-generated ``pkgsign-manifest.json`` file to "
"create the signature. You can read more about this manifest file at :ref:"
"`reference_extensions_package_signing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:213
msgid "Verifying packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_openssl.rst:215
msgid "For verifying the recipe and package, use the dedicated command:"
